1
00:06:11,612 --> 00:06:17,612
Return to Pandora.

2
00:12:23,225 --> 00:12:29,225
Avatar: The Way of Water is a action, adventure, science
fiction film directed by James Cameron.

3
00:18:34,838 --> 00:18:40,838
Set more than a decade after the events of the first film, learn the story of the Sully family (Jake, Neytiri, and their kids), the trouble that
follows them, the lengths they go to keep each other safe, the battles they fight to stay alive, and the tragedies they endure.

4
00:24:46,451 --> 00:24:52,451
Jake Sully, played by Sam Worthington.

5
00:30:58,064 --> 00:31:04,064
Neytiri, played by Zoe Saldaña.

6
00:37:09,677 --> 00:37:15,677
Kiri, played by Sigourney Weaver.

7
00:43:21,290 --> 00:43:27,290
Colonel Miles Quaritch, played by Stephen Lang.

8
00:49:32,903 --> 00:49:38,903
Ronal, played by Kate Winslet.

9
00:55:44,516 --> 00:55:50,516
Tonowari, played by Cliff Curtis.

10
01:01:56,129 --> 01:02:02,129
Avatar: The Way of Water is a 2022 American epic science fiction film directed by
James Cameron and written by Cameron, Rick Jaffa and Amanda Silver.

11
01:08:07,741 --> 01:08:13,741
It is the second in the Avatar film series.

12
01:14:19,354 --> 01:14:25,354
Sam Worthington, Zoe Saldaña and Stephen Lang reprise their roles from the first film, with
Sigourney Weaver returning in an additional role and Kate Winslet joining the cast.

13
01:20:30,967 --> 01:20:36,967
The plot follows Jake Sully, a human-turned-Na'vi, and
his family on the habitable moon Pandora.

14
01:26:42,580 --> 01:26:48,580
Hunted by RDA forces, they flee to an oceanic region to
seek refuge with the Metkayina clan.

15
01:32:54,193 --> 01:33:00,193
Following the success of Avatar in 2009, two sequels were
announced, with the first aiming for a 2014 release.

16
01:39:05,806 --> 01:39:11,806
However, the addition of two more sequels—for a total of five films—and the need to develop new
technology to film performance capture scenes underwater, led to significant delays.

17
01:45:17,419 --> 01:45:23,419
The filming process, which occurred simultaneously with the third film in the franchise,
Avatar: Fire and Ash, began in Manhattan Beach, California, on August 15, 2017.

18
01:51:29,032 --> 01:51:35,032
Production moved to Wellington, New Zealand the following month, and
was completed three years later, in September 2020.

19
01:57:40,645 --> 01:57:46,645
With an estimated budget of $350–460 million, Avatar: The Way of
Water is one of the most expensive films ever made.

20
02:03:52,258 --> 02:03:58,258
It was produced by Cameron's company Lightstorm Entertainment.

21
02:10:03,870 --> 02:10:09,870
After repeated delays in release, Avatar: The Way of Water premiered at the Odeon Leicester Square theater in London
on December 6, 2022, and was released in the United States on December 16, by 20th Century Studios.

22
02:16:15,483 --> 02:16:21,483
The film received generally positive reviews from critics, who praised the visual
effects and technical achievements but criticized the runtime.

23
02:22:27,096 --> 02:22:33,096
It was a major box office success, breaking multiple records.

24
02:28:38,709 --> 02:28:44,709
It grossed $2.320 billion in its first theatrical run, becoming the
highest-grossing film of 2022 and the third-highest-grossing film of all time.

25
02:34:50,322 --> 02:34:56,322
Among its many accolades, it was named one of the top-ten films of 2022 by
The National Board of Review and the American Film Institute.

26
02:41:01,935 --> 02:41:07,935
It was also nominated for four awards at the 95th Academy Awards,
including Best Picture, and won for Best Visual Effects.

27
02:47:13,548 --> 02:47:19,548
Fire and Ash was released in 2025.

28
02:53:25,161 --> 02:53:31,161
Two additional sequels are scheduled to be
released in 2029 and 2031, respectively.

29
02:59:36,774 --> 02:59:42,774
The film explores themes of dying and death, loss of loved one,
alien life-form, resurrection, dysfunctional family.

30
03:05:48,387 --> 03:05:54,387
The tone is lighthearted and thought_provoking.
